@bank all
// Head writer 0607: the bow lounge bar (player engineer 6's bar order; the sim engineer's bartender rota, two galley
// hands, 17:30-23:00). bar.ask/usual/serve/broke/tap are said by the bartender on the card; the rest are TEXTS.
// {drink} is the drink's name in lower case ("tea", "cocoa").

== bar.ask
- What'll it be?
- Evening. What can I get you?
- {hi}. What are you having?
- Right, what's it to be?
- Long day? What'll it be?
? tier>=friend
- Oh, it's you. What'll it be, {nick}?   #warm

== bar.usual
- The usual? A {drink}?
- Another {drink}? Coming up before you ask.
- Let me guess. {drink}.   #funny

== bar.serve
- One {drink}. Enjoy.
- There you go. One {drink}, nice and fresh.
- Here's your {drink}. Find a stool, put your feet up.
- Here you are. Careful, it's full.

// patch #29 (cocoa at the bar, with the mug in your hands: #30): cocoa's own serve line, on the card
== bar.serve.cocoa
- One cocoa. Careful, it's hot.

== bar.broke
- Bit short? Come back when you've a few more credits.
- Not enough credits, sorry. Water's free, though.

== bar.tap
- Tap night! The drink of the week is {drink}. Go on.
- Drink of the week: {drink}. I'm very proud of it.   #funny

== bar.drink.tea
- Tea
== bar.drink.juice
- Juice
== bar.drink.fizz
- Fizz
== bar.drink.cocoa
- Cocoa

== bar.closed
- Back at 17:30.

// patch #30 (the mug in your hands): drunk as you go, and Put down (TEXTS)
== bar.finish.cocoa
- You finish your cocoa. Warm all the way down.

== bar.finish.tea
- You finish your tea.

== bar.putdown
- You set your mug down. Someone will clear it.

== bar.order
- Order a drink (2 credits)

// Gym club (the player engineer's "you're a member"; the traditions engineer's rename)
== gym.member
- You're a Gym club member: this machine is yours.

== gym.yield
- Oh, go on. I'll take the next one.
- All yours. I'll hop on the bike.
- You have it. I need the rest anyway.   #funny

// the Tiles table in the junior common room, any evening
== tiles.anytime
- Tiles? Go on, then. Quick game.
- A game? You're on. Prepare to lose.   #funny
- Sure. I'll even let you go first.
